{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310692,"nonce":"Y+6hvggH7moRYHtK65aap26Bk8Y=","title":"rpkg extern class static methods (like CommandEncoder.create) route to wrong function because stdlib mapping lookup is nested inside ...","message":"rpkg extern class methods (CommandEncoder.create, etc.) are misrouted because:\n\n1. `maybe_func_id` (line 8861 hir_to_mir.rs) returns None — no function stub exists for rpkg method symbols\n2. The stdlib mapping lookup (lines 8877-8963) is INSIDE the `if let Some(func_id) = maybe_func_id { }` block\n3. When maybe_func_id is None, the else branch (line 9971+) does Dynamic-style dispatch, which picks up the wrong function\n\n**Why:** The stdlib mapping lookup should also run when maybe_func_id is None.\n\n**How to apply:** Add a stdlib mapping check at the top of the else branch (line 9971) using `find_receiver_class_name` + `stdlib_mapping.find_by_name_and_params`. This is the same pattern used in the static call path at line 9564+.\n\n**Also:** The `replace(\"::\", \"_\")` → `split(\"::\").join(\"_\")` fix was applied globally in hir_to_mir.rs to prevent double-underscore native names.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_rpkg_extern_dispatch` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}